  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia: Improving Living Conditions of Conflict and Disaster Affected Populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia continues to be affected by conflict and disasters related to natural hazards. Although there have been improvements to the peace and security situation in Somalia, the overall situation remains fragile. Forced displacement continues due to armed conflict, climate change and natural disasters. Based on the context analysis, armed-conflict, natural disasters and increasingly, climate-related crises are expected to remain key drivers of humanitarian needs. While the international community is increasingly focusing on recovery and durable solutions, needs for immediate life-saving assistance remain vast, as per the Humanitarian Needs Overview, and Humanitarian Response Plan. The main objective of this project is to ensure dignified, safe and secure living conditions and basic services for vulnerable populations affected by conflict and disasters, in particular the current drought in Somalia. IOM proposes an integrated emergency support intervention, including camp coordination and camp management, Displacement Tracking Matrix, shelter and non-food item and water, sanitation and hygiene support.</narrative>
  </description>
